//  PETPORTS -- POISON BLOCK MODULE EFFECT
//
//  The status effect half of the poison module. Its script grants
//  poisonStatusImmunity and nothing else; see the .lua for why the resistance
//  stat vanilla pairs with it is left out.
//
//  THIS IS ONLY HALF THE MODULE. A status effect can stop poison hurting a unit
//  that is standing in poison. It cannot get the unit there -- the petport
//  refuses to deploy into a liquid the chassis avoids, and it decides that with
//  no unit in the world to carry an effect. The other half is
//  petports_moduleLiquids on the item, which the port reads directly.
//
//  NO icon AND NO label, UNLIKE vanilla's poisonblock. Those drive the status
//  bar on a PLAYER. This is held by a monster under a persistent category, where
//  nothing draws them, and inventing an icon path that does not exist is a
//  missing-asset warning for no benefit. poisonblockaugment omits them too, for
//  the same reason.
//
//  defaultDuration IS UNREAD ON THE PATH WE USE. The port applies this with
//  status.setPersistentEffects, which holds it for as long as it is in the set.
//  It is stated anyway, at vanilla's value, so that an effect applied some other
//  way later behaves like the thing it was copied from rather than expiring
//  instantly. Same reasoning as petports_module_light.

{
	"name" : "petports_module_poisonblock",

	"effectConfig" : {},

	"defaultDuration" : 60,

	"scripts" : [
		"petports_module_poisonblock.lua"
	]
}
